    },
    "message": "Make the behavior proposals in Rust, so the propose phase needs no Python view of the people\n\nrules/behavior.rs does what propose_due does with UtilityBehaviorPolicy and\nPriorityRuleBehaviorPolicy, and _agent_view_snapshot, from the snapshot of rules/world_view.rs.\nWhat it does not know, and anything Python would raise on, says Unsupported, and the Python step\nruns. Results do not change; the coefficients are the same, in the same order of operations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
